Two retired adults live here. They wake around 07:30, are at home all day, and go to bed around 21:30. The walkthrough at 15:08 caught them in their usual afternoon routine. Almost nothing leaves the house: they take short walks but leave keys and bags inside. The bathroom items never move. The bedroom items are undisturbed.

**What changed from the parent (p_7c3e):** Two corrections driven by the latest evidence. First, object_4 was sighted at receptacle_12 (the shared desk) on day 16 at 05:00, and the claim "object_4 at receptacle_18, 8–20h" took 2 againsts since the last call. The pattern suggests that in the very early morning (before the couple fully wakes and starts kitchen routines), object_4 is temporarily at the desk—perhaps being wiped down or set out for the day. I have added a weekday 0–8h block placing object_4 at receptacle_12, while keeping the 8–20h block at receptacle_18. Second, object_26's claim "at receptacle_10, 9–21h" has accumulated 19 againsts versus only 10 fors; the per-object data shows object_26 is mostly at receptacle_11 (9/17 sighted days), not receptacle_10. I have moved object_26's primary block to receptacle_11 (the entryway/foyer area) for the waking day.

What sets this apart: object_4 is at the desk in the pre-dawn/early-morning window (weekday 0–8h) before moving to the kitchen shelf for the rest of the day. object_26 lives at the entryway (receptacle_11), not the living room. object_2 and object_13 remain permanently in-house. What would refute it: object_4 found at receptacle_18 before 08:00 on a weekday, or object_26 found at receptacle_10 during 10:00–18:00.

