# p_3f7d — Overnight parking: desk items consolidate at the storage shelf from midnight to 07:00

Two residents live here. During the day, desk items (object_21, object_24) and storage-shelf items (object_19, object_20, object_23) are distributed across the desk (receptacle_12) and the storage shelf (receptacle_19). But at night, between roughly 22:00 and 07:00, the residents do a brief tidy-up: they pull the desk items off the desk and park them on the storage shelf alongside the items that already live there. This creates a "consolidated shelf" state where object_19, object_20, object_21, object_23, and object_24 are all at receptacle_19 simultaneously.

The evidence: the mixture's worst-objects list shows object_21 at receptacle_19 (day 16 04:00), object_24 at receptacle_19 (day 16 00:00), object_23 at receptacle_19 (day 16 00:00), object_19 at receptacle_19 (day 16 00:00), and object_20 at receptacle_19 (day 16 06:00). These are all in the 00:00–07:00 window. During the day, object_21 is mostly at receptacle_12 (11/17 days) and object_24 is mostly at receptacle_12 (6/17 days), so the overnight shift to receptacle_19 is a real relocation, not their normal position.

What sets this apart: (1) object_21 and object_24 are at receptacle_19 (not receptacle_12) from 00:00 to 07:00. (2) This is a nightly routine, not a one-time event. (3) The items return to the desk after 07:00. What would refute it: object_21 or object_24 found at receptacle_12 during 01:00–05:00, or object_21 found at receptacle_19 during weekday 10:00–16:00.

