The revised model: both residents work from home in two focused blocks (08:00–11:00 and 15:00–18:00) with a long midday break (11:00–15:00) during which object_14 is put away on the storage shelf (receptacle_19). During the 9–17h window this gives: at the desk 9–11 (2h) + 15–17 (2h) = 4h; at the shelf 11–15 (4h) = 4h. That is exactly 50/50, matching the observed 7-found / 7-not-found split. The rest of the household routine is unchanged: object_4 on the kitchen shelf, object_15 and object_16 on the counter, nothing leaves the house.

